1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Now one-on-one with the goalkeeper.

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:06,500
Look, Roberto! This is the goal!

3
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:07,460
I'll catch it!

4
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:10,090
This time I will score!

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,720
As Roberto said, I will become a midfielder who can score goals.

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:18,600
I won't let you score!

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:24,980
My leg...

8
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,650
Because I collided with Schneider...

9
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,990
I can't take a powerful shot.

10
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:35,740
What happened to Tsubasa?

11
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:37,790
He stopped in a shooting position.

12
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:39,120
What's wrong, Tsubasa?

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,500
Shoot, Tsubasa.

14
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:42,000
Tsubasa!

15
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:45,960
I understand, his collision with Schneider...

16
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,630
Don't give up, Tsubasa!

17
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,510
I know that word isn't in your vocabulary.

18
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:52,220
Think of your next move!

19
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,100
Müller comes charging!

20
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:58,890
Why isn't Tsubasa shooting?

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:04,400
Tsubasa, football is a game of moments. Make a decision and execute it.

22
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:08,520
Oh, and Tsubasa will now shoot!

23
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:10,030
I'll catch it!

24
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,160
What?

25
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,990
This is not a shot.

26
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,910
He traps the ball with his foot.

27
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:20,160
And with centrifugal force, he passes backward!

28
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,370
This is a reverse somersault pass.

29
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:23,670
That's right, Tsubasa!

30
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,420
From here, I can't get my shot past Müller.

31
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,670
I trust you, Japan's true best forward, Kojiro Hyuga.

32
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,180
- Please, Hyuga!
- Okay.

33
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:40,180
Japan's best forward, Kojiro Hyuga, is coming.

34
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:44,100
Tsubasa created this goal opportunity all by himself.

35
00:01:44,730 --> 00:01:48,690
An opportunity like this against Germany might not come again.

36
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:52,440
I'm putting all my strength into this moment.

37
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:57,530
Catch, here it comes. This is the New Tiger Shot with all my might!

38
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:00,540
Kojiro!

39
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:06,540
Kojiro Hyuga receives Tsubasa's final pass and takes a one-touch shot!

40
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,790
Shoot, I'll stop it even if my body is torn apart!

41
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,300
But Schneider steps in front.

42
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:14,050
Get out of the way, Schneider!

43
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:17,430
I will destroy whatever is in my path.

44
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:20,560
Oh, my leg.

45
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:23,060
This shot...

46
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:26,810
...is my new Tiger!

47
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:33,940
Hyuga's terrifying shot breaks through Schneider's block and continues on its way!

48
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:49,040
Go- Goal!

49
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:55,130
Müller resisted for a moment, but finally gave in.

50
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:59,340
Hyuga's New Tiger Shot went directly into the German goal.

51
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:04,520
Ten minutes of the second half have passed, and Japan leads 2-1.

52
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,730
Your shot was great, Hyuga!

53
00:03:06,810 --> 00:03:08,270
Yes!

54
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:14,320
That's it! I was standing on the field to score this goal!

55
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,530
At the start of the second half.

56
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:20,110
The Japanese youth withstood Germany's fierce attack.

57
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:26,870
Tsubasa created the position, and with Hyuga's goal, they made it 2-1.

58
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,870
Are you okay, Tsubasa?

59
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:34,880
Yes, my collision with Schneider numbed my leg.

60
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:39,970
That's why Schneider was thrown off.

61
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:47,020
This is just like our match.

62
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:51,230
When we collided in our first encounter, our legs went numb.

63
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,900
Yes.

64
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:56,730
Your shot was great, Hyuga! Your pass was great, Tsubasa!

65
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:00,910
Now it's 2-1, and we finally took the lead by a goal.

66
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:05,280
We did it. We finally took the lead, Roberto.

67
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,910
Roberto, I know you're somewhere in the stands.

68
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,870
I did it.

69
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:17,800
Incredible, Tsubasa. That goal was exactly like page 52.

70
00:04:18,670 --> 00:04:22,010
Tsubasa, football is freedom.

71
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:25,810
Japan has finally taken a one-goal lead.

72
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,430
Against Germany, the championship contenders.

73
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:34,650
Japan is very close to victory.

74
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:38,440
I swear, I will get revenge for this.

75
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:15,360
Finally, Japan has taken a 2-1 lead!

76
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:21,030
Japan's goal put them ahead by one, and the tables have turned.

77
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:21,120
The Japan team showed tremendous effort against Germany, the holders of the championship title.

78
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:24,330
This is a huge step towards victory!

79
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:27,210
And this important goal...

80
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:30,830
...was scored by Japan's star forward and spearhead, Hyuga Kojiro.

81
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:34,210
Don't forget, the one who contributed to this goal being scored...

82
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,840
...was Captain Ozora Tsubasa.

83
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:39,760
Tsubasa, you're almost there.

84
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,800
Hang in there, Tsubasa.

85
00:06:41,890 --> 00:06:47,230
You've almost reached your dream of becoming number one in the world!

86
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,190
Good luck, Tsubasa!

87
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,280
Tsubasa.

88
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:09,370
I first saw Tsubasa cheering during the match against Shutetsu.

89
00:07:09,870 --> 00:07:11,960
Likewise, from that draw to victory...

90
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:15,960
...in the Under-12 National Championship.

91
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:20,220
And three consecutive years of high school national championships...

92
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:24,640
And now Japan in the International Youth Tournament.

93
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:28,890
He is so close to victory.

94
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:33,940
Tsubasa is turning his dream into reality.

95
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:36,690
I'm happy for him.

96
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:37,900
But...

97
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:42,200
What's wrong, Sanae?

98
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:46,200
The match isn't over yet.

99
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,160
We have to keep cheering them on.

100
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:50,460
Yes.

101
00:08:03,090 --> 00:08:06,800
And Germany restarts the match.

102
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,230
Still...

103
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,860
My leg is numb...

104
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,320
Let's advance.

105
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:23,450
All Germans.

106
00:08:23,530 --> 00:08:27,120
To protect their long-standing pride and European football championships...

107
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,620
...they attack fiercely.

108
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,870
This is a psychological battle! Don't lose to them!

109
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:31,870
Okay!

110
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:35,500
Soda! Go left! Kaltz is going there!

111
00:08:35,790 --> 00:08:36,960
Okay!

112
00:08:43,010 --> 00:08:46,390
Ishizaki, watch out for Schneider! Whatever you do, stick to him.

113
00:08:46,590 --> 00:08:48,010
Got him.

114
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:52,520
As long as he's far, you can let him shoot.

115
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:55,770
I can catch any shot from outside the penalty area.

116
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:57,650
Keep them away from the penalty area.

117
00:08:57,730 --> 00:08:58,610
Okay!

118
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:00,150
Understood!

119
00:09:00,230 --> 00:09:03,440
Wakabayashi appears for the first time in this tournament.

120
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:08,160
With him at the center, Japan's defense bravely resists Germany's attacks.

121
00:09:08,830 --> 00:09:12,160
Wakashimazu, who guarded Japan's goal until the semifinal, is here...

122
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:18,080
...and Misugi, who scored in the semifinal against France, is here.

123
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:22,710
On this side, the Tachibana brothers, unable to play due to injuries...

124
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,260
...but they and the rest of the team on the bench...

125
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:28,220
...support the 11 players fighting on the field with their spirit.

126
00:09:28,470 --> 00:09:32,060
Japan is truly fighting in unity!

127
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,070
I won't let you pass.

128
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:52,870
Margas.

129
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,330
Matsuyama clears the ball.

130
00:10:04,050 --> 00:10:06,550
15 minutes left in the match.

131
00:10:06,630 --> 00:10:11,350
In 15 minutes, the Japanese youth could be champions.

132
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:16,850
Winning this tournament will prove that Japan has progressed incredibly.

133
00:10:17,310 --> 00:10:20,100
Right now it's 10 o'clock at night in Japan...

134
00:10:20,190 --> 00:10:23,610
...but I'm sure fans all over Japan are staying up tonight...

135
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,610
...to watch our young samurai.

136
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:29,360
15 minutes stand between Japan and victory!

137
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:39,580
Good luck, Taro.

138
00:10:44,210 --> 00:10:45,800
Because they're one goal ahead...

139
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:49,510
...Misaki is also playing defense against Germany's fierce attacks.

140
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:54,060
With Japan's strong defense, Germany has no chance.

141
00:10:56,350 --> 00:10:57,640
Are we losing?

142
00:10:57,730 --> 00:10:59,690
Are we really losing?

143
00:10:59,890 --> 00:11:02,900
Everyone calls us the best.

144
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,650
In football, it's not the strongest who wins, but the one who scores.

145
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:11,610
In football, the strongest wins.

146
00:11:12,530 --> 00:11:14,080
Schneider.

147
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:18,080
If I could just get rid of this numbness...

148
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,920
Schneider.

149
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:25,550
Good. Come on. Give it to me.

150
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:29,420
Did you get rid of your numbness with pain, Schneider?

151
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:31,340
Go, Schneider.

152
00:11:33,010 --> 00:11:35,220
The ball goes to Schneider.

153
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:37,770
Schneider attacks with anger.

154
00:11:39,430 --> 00:11:41,230
Come on, Schneider.

155
00:11:41,390 --> 00:11:44,360
Schneider goes directly toward Japan's goal!

156
00:11:44,810 --> 00:11:46,110
I'll cut him off!

157
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,190
Get out of the way!

158
00:11:49,650 --> 00:11:52,200
Misaki is thrown into the air!

159
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:56,120
Catch, here it comes, Wakabayashi.

160
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:00,660
I'll catch it.

161
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:03,170
In practice, half of them were goals.

162
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,380
That won't happen now.

163
00:12:12,010 --> 00:12:14,010
Great, Wakabayashi.

164
00:12:14,090 --> 00:12:15,260
Wakabayashi.

165
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:17,760
A magnificent performance from goalkeeper Wakabayashi.

166
00:12:17,850 --> 00:12:20,020
He doesn't allow the equalizer.

167
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,190
We must equalize first!

168
00:12:27,270 --> 00:12:29,480
We will score this goal!

169
00:12:29,570 --> 00:12:32,740
Germany's fierce attack resumes.

170
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:34,360
They're coming again!

171
00:12:34,450 --> 00:12:35,990
Whatever you do, stand firm.

172
00:12:36,070 --> 00:12:37,490
We have to press them immediately.

173
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:47,000
My Ryo. I can't believe Ryo is playing in the jersey with the Japanese flag.

174
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:50,710
All of this is thanks to Tsubasa.

175
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,380
Mrs. Ishizaki.

176
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:58,970
Tsubasa made my son what he is today.

177
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:04,940
I'm proud of him. I'm very happy.

178
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:10,110
No, this happened because of Ishizaki's hard work.

179
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:21,700
There!

180
00:13:21,790 --> 00:13:24,620
Matsuyama clears the ball.

181
00:13:24,710 --> 00:13:27,460
Another great defense from Japan.

182
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:33,460
We thought Japan wouldn't win a single match in this tournament.

183
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:40,100
Match after match, every time they played against one of us, they grew stronger.

184
00:13:40,470 --> 00:13:47,440
And now Japan has grown strong enough to beat Germany, the perennial champions.

185
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:51,980
Japanese football will continue to grow stronger!

186
00:13:52,230 --> 00:13:56,610
Our football intends to leave its mark on the world.

187
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:01,410
What?

188
00:14:01,490 --> 00:14:05,120
But the artist on the field, Misaki, gets the ball.

189
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,000
Tsubasa!

190
00:14:07,210 --> 00:14:08,750
Great, Misaki!

191
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:11,630
The ball comes to playmaker and captain Tsubasa.

192
00:14:11,710 --> 00:14:14,010
Finally, Japan is attacking.

193
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:17,260
Come on, Tsubasa! Let's score another goal.

194
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:19,140
Here, Hyuga!

195
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,640
- What?
- How fast!

196
00:14:27,230 --> 00:14:28,060
Kaltz!

197
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:30,150
He spit out his gum!

198
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:32,900
Alright, let's go at them.

199
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:37,400
They may be famous for their Japanese spirit, but we have the German spirit.

200
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:41,780
10 minutes left. Now it's our turn to show our German spirit.

201
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:45,540
Guys, Kaltz is right! Follow Kaltz!

202
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:46,790
I'll cut him off!

203
00:14:46,870 --> 00:14:49,790
Get out of my way. Move.

204
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,880
Hedgehog Dribble.

205
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:55,210
Wow, Kaltz has gotten serious.

206
00:14:57,800 --> 00:15:02,390
Even with this dribble, I can't get past the defense.

207
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:05,310
To get past the Japanese defense, you have to dive in and pass to the side.

208
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:06,560
Schester!

209
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,930
Ah, it's a pass.

210
00:15:08,230 --> 00:15:10,350
Kaltz is right. 10 minutes left.

211
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,440
Time to show our true strength.

212
00:15:13,650 --> 00:15:14,770
What?

213
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:17,690
Schester switches the field with a pass!

214
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,320
Great, Schester. I'll take it from here.

215
00:15:20,490 --> 00:15:21,450
Will he go left?

216
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:23,450
Wait! Go to Kaltz!

217
00:15:23,530 --> 00:15:25,830
He is Germany's key player right now.

218
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:26,950
Okay.

219
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,960
The rest is up to you, Kaltz.

220
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:31,500
Clever Wakabayashi. You figured it out well.

221
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:34,590
But it's too late now. I'll leave him to you.

222
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:36,340
Go, Schneider.

223
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:38,510
Oh, Kaltz left the ball.

224
00:15:38,590 --> 00:15:39,590
What?

225
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:42,090
No! Kaltz fooled us.

226
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,010
Now Schneider is free.

227
00:15:45,390 --> 00:15:49,980
It's impossible for the likes of Japan to tarnish Germany's enduring championship.

228
00:15:50,230 --> 00:15:53,060
We protect our sacred history.

229
00:15:53,150 --> 00:15:55,230
Watch the German spirit!

230
00:15:56,150 --> 00:15:57,780
Fire!

231
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,860
Time for courage!

232
00:16:01,950 --> 00:16:07,330
This is my ultimate Face Block!

233
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,330
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

234
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,860
Birthday: March 24 | Height: 162 cm | Weight: 55 kg | Blood Type: O

235
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,700
Time for courage!

236
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:20,500
This is my ultimate Face Block!

237
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:24,170
What?

238
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:31,010
Ishizaki!

239
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:32,010
Ryo!

240
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:33,510
Ishizaki!

241
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:42,270
Schneider, the ball is still in play above you.

242
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:45,770
When I land, I'll shoot again.

243
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:49,150
Would I let Ishizaki's courage go to waste?

244
00:16:49,190 --> 00:16:50,900
I'll cut it off, Schneider.

245
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:53,650
I won't allow it. I'll clear the ball first.

246
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:56,280
Will Matsuyama head it clear?

247
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,780
Here, Schneider!

248
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:01,410
Margas reaches it first and passes with a header.

249
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,000
Thanks, Margas.

250
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:07,250
Catch, here it comes, Wakabayashi! This is the equalizer!

251
00:17:10,590 --> 00:17:11,420
I'll stop it!

252
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,010
Tsubasa!

253
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:18,600
What?

254
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:21,140
Tsubasa goes to block the shot!

255
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:24,060
Schneider slips past Tsubasa's challenge with perfect timing!

256
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:27,900
Face Block!

257
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,150
Watch out, Tsubasa!

258
00:17:29,230 --> 00:17:31,690
From the side, he leaps backward.

259
00:17:33,530 --> 00:17:34,610
Impossible!

260
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,610
Great. I knew you'd do that.

261
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:39,950
Schneider faked a shot a second time.

262
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:42,370
But this time, will he shoot with his left foot?

263
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:44,710
Good. Tsubasa is out!

264
00:17:44,790 --> 00:17:46,330
Now it's your turn, Wakabayashi.

265
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,590
Is Schneider shooting with his left foot?

266
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:52,000
Or is it another fake? Which one?

267
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:53,420
Fire Feint!

268
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:06,100
He couldn't catch it! In the net! Goal!

269
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,770
In the 22nd minute of the second half, Schneider shot with his left foot.

270
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,730
And it went into the goal from the left side!

271
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:13,900
Even the great Wakabayashi couldn't catch it this time.

272
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:20,240
Germany finally equalized!

273
00:18:20,490 --> 00:18:21,950
Well done, Captain!

274
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:25,040
This is our German spirit!

275
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:27,540
Your shot was great, Schneider!

276
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,920
You gave me this opportunity.

277
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:33,300
As captain, it's impossible for me to let you down.

278
00:18:34,250 --> 00:18:36,590
Wakabayashi knows my right foot well.

279
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:42,180
So my left foot surprised him for a moment.

280
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:44,890
Alright, get ready, guys!

281
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:47,020
We keep going and take the lead.

282
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:48,190
Okay!

283
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:52,940
Damn. I hesitated for a moment.

284
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:56,940
Ishizaki!

285
00:18:58,030 --> 00:18:59,450
Ishizaki, are you okay?

286
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:05,160
- Ishizaki!
- Hang in there!

287
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:07,080
Ishizaki!

288
00:19:10,290 --> 00:19:11,710
Ishizaki!

289
00:19:13,380 --> 00:19:17,840
No. I feel dizzy.

290
00:19:18,510 --> 00:19:22,890
And I have no strength left.

291
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:26,020
Something might be broken.

292
00:19:26,430 --> 00:19:28,600
Don't move, Ishizaki.

293
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:31,940
Damn, did they tie it up?

294
00:19:32,190 --> 00:19:35,940
For the first time, I was useful...

295
00:19:36,570 --> 00:19:37,900
Ishizaki.

296
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,200
Tsubasa.

297
00:19:42,530 --> 00:19:44,950
I always wanted to tell you.

298
00:19:45,330 --> 00:19:46,910
Thank you.

299
00:19:47,410 --> 00:19:52,460
Being able to come this far is entirely thanks to you.

300
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,460
I'm very happy.

301
00:19:55,540 --> 00:20:00,260
That I met you, Tsubasa.

302
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:04,760
Now I'm representing Japan...

303
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:09,600
...and I'm a full member of the team.

304
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:18,280
My football dream came true a long time ago.

305
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,360
Ishizaki.

306
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:24,110
But Tsubasa, please.

307
00:20:24,490 --> 00:20:29,790
My dream now is for you to become the best footballer in the world.

308
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:34,750
Don't let me down. Okay, Tsubasa?

309
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:37,210
What are you saying, Ishizaki?

310
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:41,550
This isn't just my dream, it's everyone's dream.

311
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:45,840
That's right.

312
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:51,100
But for me, it ends here.

313
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:53,730
Ishizaki!

314
00:20:53,810 --> 00:20:55,440
- Ishizaki.
- Ishizaki!

315
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,190
Hold on, Ishizaki.

316
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:58,860
Coach Sumitomo!

317
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,320
Take Ishizaki to the infirmary!

318
00:21:00,610 --> 00:21:01,530
Yes, Head Coach.

319
00:21:01,610 --> 00:21:03,070
Izawa, you're on.

320
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,320
Yes.

321
00:21:06,450 --> 00:21:09,160
Ishizaki is carried off on a stretcher.

322
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:11,330
We are all worried about him.

323
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:13,080
Ryo.

324
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:16,380
I'm sure he'll recover.

325
00:21:16,670 --> 00:21:20,880
Japan sends Izawa on for Ishizaki.

326
00:21:22,210 --> 00:21:24,510
Goalkeeper Wakabayashi

327
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:27,090
7 minutes left in the match, and we're back to square one.

328
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:27,260
Defender Matsuyama

329
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:27,260
Defender Jito

330
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:29,470
Midfielder Sano

331
00:21:27,340 --> 00:21:29,470
Midfielder Sawada

332
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:32,020
Which team will score the winning goal?

333
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:32,020
Midfielder Tsubasa

334
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:32,020
Midfielder Misaki

335
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:35,020
Forward Nitta

336
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:35,020
Forward Hyuga

337
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:35,020
No one can predict.

338
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,520
Midfielder Schester

339
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,520
Forward Margas

340
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,520
Forward Schneider

341
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,520
Defensive Midfielder

342
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,520
Defensive Midfielder Kaltz

343
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:40,520
Right now, it's about mental strength.

344
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,280
Defender Hein

345
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,280
Defender Mayer

346
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,280
Defender Hardwich

347
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,280
Defender Magath

348
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,280
Defender Mylus

349
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:43,280
This is Japanese spirit versus German spirit.

350
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,570
Goalkeeper Müller

351
00:21:43,570 --> 00:21:47,530
As representatives of Germany, we can't lose to Japan!

352
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:48,870
Right!

353
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:53,000
Guys, don't forget Ishizaki's courage.

354
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:58,540
He may not be on the field, but his spirit is in our hearts.

355
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,630
The match is tied, and we start from here.

356
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:05,050
We will be the ones to score the winning goal.

357
00:22:05,090 --> 00:22:06,510
Yes!